INTENTIONAL. Ronin's `$(MAKEFLAGS)` reads back the text it stores, so a `$` a
switch value carried arrives doubled where GNU Make 4.4.1 halves it. Decided on
make-makeflags-holds-its-switches-as-literal-text and recorded in
docs/make-oracle-divergences.md; the sibling case
`a-child-keeps-a-switch-value-a-dollar-was-written-in` measures what GNU Make's
halving costs. Not a defect to be repaired — a change that made this case pass
would take that one with it.
